#[serde(rename_all = "camelCase")]
pub enum EntryState {
    Streaming,
    Complete,
    /// The answer was stopped before it was finished.
    Interrupted,
    /// The answer reached its bound; the rest was not kept.
    Truncated,
    Failed,
    /// The operator declined it, or it was refused (C21).
    Declined,
}

/// What an engine request for approval asks (C21).
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, TS)]
#[serde(rename_all = "camelCase")]
pub enum ApprovalKind {
    /// Run one command in the project's sandbox.
    Command,
    /// Change files in the project.
    FileChange,
    /// Call one tool of a workspace MCP server, once (C22).
    McpTool,
    /// Read the tenant through one of the desktop's own read tools, once
    /// (C32): read-only by construction.
    DesktopRead,
}

/// What a decision lets the engine do, as the core can establish it (C32).
/// Only a desktop read, or a command in a read-only project sandbox, is
/// read-only; a file change, a command with changes allowed and any remote
/// MCP tool (whose effect the desktop cannot know) may change things, and
/// allowing one needs the native confirmation, never in-page consent alone.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, TS)]
#[serde(rename_all = "camelCase")]
pub enum ApprovalEffect {
    ReadOnly,
    MayChange,
}

/// A pending approval, as the operator sees it (C21). Its id is the
/// desktop's own, issued for this run and turn; it never outlives them.
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, TS)]
#[serde(rename_all = "camelCase")]
pub struct HarnessApproval {
    pub id: String,
                )?
            }
            "cases" => {
                let _: Empty = serde_json::from_value(args).ok()?;
                Self::Cases
            }
            "mcpServers" => {
                let _: Empty = serde_json::from_value(args).ok()?;
                Self::McpServers
            }
            "proposeChange" => {
                let a: ProposeArgs = serde_json::from_value(args).ok()?;
                // The Runtime and DLP kinds (create, update, delete); an API
                // key's version, the start of a rotation the operator
                // finishes in Administration (C32); and a guardrail of the
                // conversation's own Gateway workspace, created or updated,
                // reviewed under that workspace (C32). Nothing else.
                let runtime = matches!(
                    a.kind,
                    ChangeKind::Profiles
                        | ChangeKind::Topics
                        | ChangeKind::Applications
                        | ChangeKind::ApiKeys
                        | ChangeKind::DataPatterns
                        | ChangeKind::DataProfiles
                        | ChangeKind::FilteringProfiles
                        | ChangeKind::Dictionaries
                ) && matches!(
                    a.action,
                    ChangeAction::Create | ChangeAction::Update | ChangeAction::Delete
                );
                let rotation = a.kind == ChangeKind::ApiKeys && a.action == ChangeAction::Version;
                let guardrail = a.kind == ChangeKind::GatewayGuardrails
                    && matches!(a.action, ChangeAction::Create | ChangeAction::Update);
                if !(runtime || rotation || guardrail)
                    || a.summary.trim().is_empty()
                    || a.summary.chars().count() > 512
                    || a.target.len() > 256
                    || a.target.chars().any(char::is_control)
                {
                    return None;
                }
                let body = Value::Object(a.body.unwrap_or_default()).to_string();
                Self::ProposeChange {
                    kind: a.kind,
                    action: a.action,
                    target: a.target,
                    body,
                    summary: a.summary.chars().filter(|c| !c.is_control()).collect(),
                }
            }
            _ => return None,
        };
# C31 — Reviews, Administration inventory, key rotation

Phase: P09. Status: planned. Required predecessor: C30.

## Outcome

Configuration reviews bind tenant, resource and typed name in the core; Administration renders from an inventory with per-tab capabilities; key rotation is a three-stage flow with one-time secret disclosure through the host.

## Inputs and dependency gates

C30; screens/reviews-administration.md. Read the [common execution contract](../IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md),
[review protocol](../review-protocol.md), and [test catalogue](../test-catalogue.md).
Read the [UI v2 specification](../../architecture/ui-v2/DESIGN-V2.md) and its
companions; the frozen prototype under `docs/architecture/ui-v2/prototype/` is
an immutable input. Freeze all source/shared dependency inputs.

## Milestones

1. Scopes `Review`, `AdminInventory` (every tab mapped to an admitted `ManagementResource`/`GatewayRead`/C13 read and every action to an admitted `ChangeKind`+`ChangeAction`; AIS and AES unavailable with their gate), topic inventory with distinct detector/topic key types; intents `openReview`, `confirmReview{typed}`, `acknowledgeDeployment`; key rotation is the admitted sequence `ApiKeys·Version` → local acknowledgement → `ApiKeys·Delete` with readback; the issued secret uses the existing `RevealSecret`/`ForgetSecret` host path, is never persisted, and is dropped on every review exit including tenant switch and context retirement.
2. Administration accordion and tables; review surface with diff, impact, typed name, applied panels; rotation panel states 1–4 (screens/reviews-administration.md); rotation reminder as a distinct Inbox item; two labelled timestamps (deployment acknowledged, old key removed) stored once; unknown outcomes shown as unconfirmed with reconciliation.

